if BOARD_CB91AI

config CB91AI_PROVISION_UICR
	bool "Program UICR at first boot (REGOUT0 = 3.0 V, debug port kept open)"
	default y
	help
	  VDD of the nRF52840 is fed by the coin cell while VDDH is fed by USB.
	  When USB is plugged the chip enters high voltage mode and REG0 drives
	  the 3V rail at the voltage stored in UICR.REGOUT0, whose factory value
	  is 1.8 V. This option programs REGOUT0 to 3.0 V and, on revision 3 or
	  later dies only (build code F and up, hardened APPROTECT), sets
	  UICR.APPROTECT to HwDisabled (0x5A) so that the SWD port stays open.
	  On older dies (build codes up to D, legacy APPROTECT) UICR.APPROTECT
	  is left erased, which is the only value keeping the port open there.
	  The chip is reset once after programming.

endif # BOARD_CB91AI
